A||||3||JSocha||Cylinder compression values.  Whats considered good/bad? Target values?||||5||
Z||000000||JSocha||09-26-2001||02:43 PM||||Just went to the mechanic who is looking over the 86 GT I picked up in Texas.<P>As I am not mechanically inclined:<P>All 6 cylinders are running between 135 to 140/145 for compression according to the mechanic and said that the motor is strong.<P>I searched in the Tech and GFC areas to see if someone posted compression values to target for for durability.  <P>Loyde R. of Texas had told me what to look for, but it was dark out, therefore I didn't write the values he stated down and now have forgot what he said.<P>What should one hopefully shoot for: 130 ok; 140 good; 150 best; 160 excellant; 170 outstanding?  What?!?!?!?  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/confused.gif"><P>How do you guys rate it?<P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/jsocha_2.gif"> ||||reg||5
Z||000001||lou_dias||09-26-2001||03:16 PM||||anything near 100 or less is considered low per my 86 service manual,<P>140 is good||||reg||1
Z||000002||PBJ||09-26-2001||03:17 PM||||the important factor about a compression test<BR>is that they are all the same, or close to it<BR>not so much how high they are. But 130 is good.<P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/forsalestart.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000003||Capt Fiero||09-26-2001||05:55 PM||||my brand new motor has 165-175 and that is above normal compression.  So if you are at 140 or so with a stock 5-10 year old motor, you are doing pretty good||||reg||1
